# Verse & Vale — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values. `.env` is gitignored
# (see .gitignore: .env and .env.* are ignored, this .env.example is not),
# so your real credentials never get committed.
#
# These are SERVER-SIDE ONLY. They are read exclusively inside the Vercel
# serverless route api/generate-cards.ts and are never imported into anything
# Vite bundles (AGENTS.md §6 permits exactly one credential in the browser
# bundle, the YouVersion app_key, and none of these are it). A test,
# src/app/glooCredentialBoundary.test.ts, asserts this boundary holds.

# --- Gloo AI (PRD-09: insight card generation) ----------------------------
# Gloo AI does NOT issue a static API key. It uses OAuth2 client-credentials:
# the route POSTs the client id/secret to
# https://platform.ai.gloo.com/oauth2/token (scope api/access), gets a
# short-lived bearer token, and uses that against the OpenAI-compatible
# inference API. The route does that exchange for you — you only supply the
# four values below. With any of them missing, the route returns `unavailable`
# and every encounter degrades to the reviewed fallback set (the same as a
# Gloo outage), so the app still runs with none of these set.

# OAuth2 client credentials from the Gloo AI Studio dashboard.
GLOO_CLIENT_ID=
GLOO_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Gloo's OpenAI-compatible inference base URL. The @ai-sdk/openai-compatible
# provider appends /chat/completions to this.
GLOO_BASE_URL=https://platform.ai.gloo.com/ai/v2

# The routing mode. Leave GLOO_MODEL_ID UNSET to use Gloo AI Core: the platform
# auto-routes each request to the optimal model (auto_routing). This is the
# default and what the game uses.
#
# To pin one specific model instead, set GLOO_MODEL_ID to a gloo-* id — see
# https://docs.gloo.com/api-guides/supported-models for the full list.
# Examples: gloo-anthropic-claude-haiku-4.5, gloo-openai-gpt-5-mini,
# gloo-anthropic-claude-sonnet-5, gloo-openai-gpt-5.2.
# GLOO_MODEL_ID=

# --- YouVersion Platform (PRD-10: sign-in, live Scripture, highlight sync) --
# `app_key` is a public OAuth client identifier, not a secret (AGENTS.md §6
# explicitly allows exactly this one credential in the browser bundle).
# Read client-side via Vite's import.meta.env, so it must be VITE_-prefixed.
# Get one at https://platform.youversion.com/. With this unset, sign-in stays
# the stub, Scripture falls back to the bundled WEB text, and highlights
# still capture locally with no sync — the same no-credentials path every
# other YouVersion-backed seam takes (see src/app/youversionConfig.ts).
VITE_YOUVERSION_APP_KEY=

# Server-side only, read inside api/youversion-token.ts. Overrides the
# YouVersion Platform API host the token exchange forwards to; almost never
# needs to be set (default: api.youversion.com).
# YOUVERSION_API_HOST=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Testing the live /api routes locally
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `pnpm dev` serves /api/* as well as the app: vite-plugin-api-routes.ts mounts
# the api/ handlers on the dev server and loads every var in this file into
# `process.env`, so the routes see the same environment they do on Vercel. Both
# the Gloo card path and YouVersion sign-in work in the browser against the real
# routes; no `vercel dev` and no Vercel login needed.
#
# This matters because both routes' clients turn any failure into a recoverable
# `unavailable`/`Result`. Before the plugin existed, /api/* 404'd under Vite and
# the symptom was silent-to-misleading: the Gloo path quietly served fallback
# cards, and sign-in reported "Couldn't connect right now" when the route had
# simply never run. A sign-in failure now also logs its real reason to the
# browser console.
#
# To hit a route directly instead of through the game:
#
#     curl -s http://localhost:5173/api/generate-cards \
#       -H 'content-type: application/json' \
#       -d '{"reference":"2KI.24.1-4","anchor":"DAN.1.1","section":"OT History",
#            "note":"Nebuchadnezzar besieged Jerusalem and the Lord gave Jehoiakim into his hand."}'
#
# A healthy live path returns {"status":"generated", ... six cards ... }.
# {"status":"unavailable", ...} means creds/model wrong or the call failed —
# check the `pnpm dev` terminal for the route's error.
